--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyleft disclosure — prebuilt libvips binaries (LGPL-3.0-or-later)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  sharp (itself Apache-2.0) redistributes prebuilt libvips binaries through
  its @img/sharp-libvips-* platform packages, which declare LGPL-3.0-or-later;
  @img/sharp-wasm32 and @img/sharp-win32-* carry an equivalent
  "Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-3.0-or-later" expression for their embedded libvips.
  These binaries enter the dependency tree in three places: as a declared
  optional dependency of the embedded lore (sharp ^0.35.3), and transitively
  under @huggingface/transformers and @lancedb/lancedb, which each carry their
  own sharp copy. LGPL-3.0-or-later is a weak copyleft: it covers the libvips
  binaries themselves, not Atlas's Apache-2.0 code — no Atlas source derives
  from libvips, and the binaries are installed unmodified from the npm
  registry rather than vendored in this repository. libvips source is
  available at https://github.com/libvips/libvips.

